'' TKO0933, fbc's 71 (T31): '*a' and 'a[ i ]' over an 'any ptr' are refused in every
'' position -- an initialiser, an assignment target, a print item, the outer '*' of '**pa',
'' an index, an argument, '@( *a )' and 'sizeof( *a )'. tiko took them all: a read gave
'' garbage, a write did nothing, a print item truncated its statement. 'cptr( long ptr,
'' a )', a typed pointer made from it and '*pa' itself are fine. Lines identical to
'' fbc-modern's errors. See symbols/anyptrderef.bas.
'' TEST: cli
